.TH APP-CHOOSER 1 2026-11-15 "aperi @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
app-chooser \- open a file or URI with the desktop application chooser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B app-chooser
.I file
|
.I uri
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B app-chooser
asks the desktop portal to open its argument, always showing the dialog to
choose the application to use.
It is meant as the last, catch all rule of the
.BR aperi (1)
configuration, to choose an application for everything without a more
specific rule:
.PP
.RS
.EX
/*=app-chooser
.EE
.RE
.PP
An argument containing
.B ://
is opened as a URI with the
.B OpenURI
method of the
.B org.freedesktop.portal.OpenURI
D-Bus interface; anything else is opened as a file with the
.B OpenFile
method.
.PP
Without arguments,
.B app-chooser
prints its version and a short usage message.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B app-chooser
exits with status 0 once the portal has answered the request, and with
status 1 if the file can't be opened, the session bus is not available or
the request can't be sent.
.SH NOTES
A running
.B xdg-desktop-portal
is needed, with a backend providing the application chooser dialog (e.g.\&
.B xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
or
.BR xdg-desktop-portal-gnome ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aperi (1)
.SH AUTHORS
Matteo Beniamino <m.beniamino@tautologica.org>
